# goosehints - Repository Standards
# UK Government Contracts Finder Java Library

## Quick Overview
- **Language**: Java (version managed by `mise`) - baseline on currently preferred LTS version of OpenJDK
- **Build Tool**: Gradle (version managed by `mise`)
- **Dependencies**: Target of ZERO external dependencies - only include if a requirement is going to introduce new code of significant complexity and there is already a well established library that solves the issue. User approval is REQUIRED prior to including external libraries.
- **JAR Size**: Optimise to be as small as possible, while maintaining readability of source code
- **Tests**: All key functionality must be covered by Unit Tests
- **Versioning**: Semantic Versioning with release-please automation
- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions with jdx-mise-action

## Key Standards

### Code Quality
- Compiler flags: `-Xlint:all -parameters -release 17`
- Full JavaDoc on public APIs
- Code style: 4-space indentation, LF endings, UTF-8 (enforced via .editorconfig)
- Exception handling: Custom exception hierarchy (ContractsFinderException, HttpException)
- Design patterns: Fluent builders, AutoCloseable resources

### Dependencies
- **Main Library**: Only JDK standard library
- **HTTP**: java.net.http.HttpClient (HTTP/2, built-in)
- **JSON**: Regex-based parser (no external library)
- **Testing**: JUnit 5 (test-only dependency)

### Build & Testing
- Build: `gradle build` (~1 second)
- Test: `gradle test` with full logging
- JAR optimization: Excluded metadata files, selective manifest entries
- Incremental compilation and build caching enabled

### Version Control & Releases
- **Commits**: Conventional Commits standard (feat:, fix:, docs:, etc.)
- **Branching**: main (releases), develop (development)
- **Releases**: Fully automated via release-please (no manual tagging)
- **Version Source**: gradle.properties (single source of truth)
- **Changelog**: CHANGELOG.md (Keep a Changelog format, auto-updated)

### GitHub Actions Workflows

**release.yml** - Triggered on push to main
- Uses jdx-mise-action for environment setup
- Runs release-please for automated releases
- Builds JAR and uploads artifacts
- Tool caching enabled (50-70% faster)

**test.yml** - Triggered on PR to main/develop
- Uses jdx-mise-action for environment setup
- Runs `gradle test --info`
- Outputs results to job summary and PR comment
- Uploads test artifacts (30-day retention)
- Tool caching enabled

### Tool Management
- **mise.toml**: Single source of truth for tool versions
- **Current Tools**: Java 17, Gradle latest
- **CI/CD Integration**: jdx-mise-action@v2 in all workflows
- **Caching**: Enabled by default (cache invalidates on mise.toml changes)

### Project Structure
```
src/main/java/com/aletheia/contractsfinder/
  ├── ContractsFinderClient.java (interface)
  ├── ContractsFinderClientImpl.java (implementation)
  ├── SearchCriteria.java (fluent builder)
  ├── Contract.java, Notice.java (data models)
  ├── http/ (HTTP layer with HttpClient, URL utils, JSON parser)
  └── module-info.java (JPMS configuration)

src/test/java/
  ├── ContractsFinderClientImplTest.java (8 tests)
  └── HttpUtilTest.java (5 tests)

.github/workflows/
  ├── release.yml (automated releases)
  └── test.yml (PR testing)

docs/
  ├── README.md (user guide)
  ├── QUICKREF.md (quick reference)
  ├── CONTRIBUTING.md (development guidelines)
  └── RELEASE_PROCESS.md (release guide)
```

## Development Workflow
1. Create feature branch from `main`
2. Write code following standards above
3. Commit with conventional commits format
4. When requested by the user, push feature branch to create PR against `main`
5. test.yml automatically runs tests
6. View results in job summary or PR comment
7. Merge PR → release.yml handles release on main

## Key Files
- `build.gradle.kts` - JAR optimization, zero dependencies
- `mise.toml` - Tool versions (Java 17, Gradle latest)
- `release-please-config.json` - Semantic versioning rules
- `.editorconfig` - Code style enforcement
- `module-info.java` - JPMS module configuration

## Testing Standards
- Framework: JUnit 5
- Execution: Via test.yml on PR or `gradle test` locally
- Coverage: Unit tests for core API and HTTP utilities
- Pass Rate: 100% is MANDATORY

## Documentation Standards
- Format: Markdown for guides, JavaDoc for APIs
- Audiences: Users (README), developers (QUICKREF, CONTRIBUTING), maintainers (RELEASE_PROCESS)
- Completeness: Always include quick start, examples, and troubleshooting

## References
- Conventional Commits: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
- Semantic Versioning: https://semver.org/
- release-please: https://github.com/googleapis/release-please
- jdx-mise-action: https://github.com/jdx/mise-action
